(Article. I.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All legislative Powers herein granted shall be vested in a Congress of the United States, which) Tj T*
(shall consist of a Senate and House of Representatives.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No Person shall be a Representative who shall not have attained to the Age of twenty five Years, and) Tj T*
(been seven Years a Citizen of the United States, and who shall not, when elected, be an Inhabitant) Tj T*
(of that State in which he shall be chosen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Senate of the United States shall be composed of two Senators from each State, chosen by the) Tj T*
(Legislature thereof, for six Years; and each Senator shall have one Vote.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The House of Representatives shall chuse their Speaker and other Officers; and shall have the sole) Tj T*
(Power of Impeachment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Senate shall have the sole Power to try all Impeachments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Congress shall have Power To lay and collect Taxes, Duties, Imposts and Excises, to pay the) Tj T*
(Debts and provide for the common Defence and general Welfare of the United States; but all Duties,) Tj T*
(Imposts and Excises shall be uniform throughout the United States;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To regulate Commerce with foreign Nations, and among the several States, and with the Indian Tribes;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To coin Money, regulate the Value thereof, and of foreign Coin, and fix the Standard of Weights and) Tj T*
(Measures;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To establish Post Offices and post Roads;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To declare War, grant Letters of Marque and Reprisal, and make Rules concerning Captures on Land and) Tj T*
(Water;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
(Evaluation fixture page 2) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
