(Article. II.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The executive Power shall be vested in a President of the United States of America. He shall hold) Tj T*
(his Office during the Term of four Years, and, together with the Vice President, chosen for the same) Tj T*
(Term, be elected, as follows) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No Person except a natural born Citizen, or a Citizen of the United States, at the time of the) Tj T*
(Adoption of this Constitution, shall be eligible to the Office of President; neither shall any) Tj T*
(Person be eligible to that Office who shall not have attained to the Age of thirty five Years, and) Tj T*
(been fourteen Years a Resident within the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The President shall be Commander in Chief of the Army and Navy of the United States, and of the) Tj T*
(Militia of the several States, when called into the actual Service of the United States; he may) Tj T*
(require the Opinion, in writing, of the principal Officer in each of the executive Departments, upon) Tj T*
(any Subject relating to the Duties of their respective Offices, and he shall have Power to grant) Tj T*
(Reprieves and Pardons for Offences against the United States, except in Cases of Impeachment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(He shall have Power, by and with the Advice and Consent of the Senate, to make Treaties, provided) Tj T*
(two thirds of the Senators present concur; and he shall nominate, and by and with the Advice and) Tj T*
(Consent of the Senate, shall appoint Ambassadors, other public Ministers and Consuls, Judges of the) Tj T*
(supreme Court, and all other Officers of the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(He shall from time to time give to the Congress Information of the State of the Union, and recommend) Tj T*
(to their Consideration such Measures as he shall judge necessary and expedient.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The President, Vice President and all civil Officers of the United States, shall be removed from) Tj T*
(Office on Impeachment for, and Conviction of, Treason, Bribery, or other high Crimes and) Tj T*
(Misdemeanors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
(Evaluation fixture page 3) Tj T*
ET
