(Article. III.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The judicial Power of the United States, shall be vested in one supreme Court, and in such inferior) Tj T*
(Courts as the Congress may from time to time ordain and establish. The Judges, both of the supreme) Tj T*
(and inferior Courts, shall hold their Offices during good Behaviour, and shall, at stated Times,) Tj T*
(receive for their Services, a Compensation, which shall not be diminished during their Continuance) Tj T*
(in Office.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The judicial Power shall extend to all Cases, in Law and Equity, arising under this Constitution,) Tj T*
(the Laws of the United States, and Treaties made, or which shall be made, under their Authority; to) Tj T*
(all Cases affecting Ambassadors, other public Ministers and Consuls; to all Cases of admiralty and) Tj T*
(maritime Jurisdiction; to Controversies to which the United States shall be a Party; to) Tj T*
(Controversies between two or more States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Trial of all Crimes, except in Cases of Impeachment, shall be by Jury; and such Trial shall be) Tj T*
(held in the State where the said Crimes shall have been committed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Treason against the United States, shall consist only in levying War against them, or in adhering to) Tj T*
(their Enemies, giving them Aid and Comfort. No Person shall be convicted of Treason unless on the) Tj T*
(Testimony of two Witnesses to the same overt Act, or on Confession in open Court.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
(Evaluation fixture page 4) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
