(Article. IV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Full Faith and Credit shall be given in each State to the public Acts, Records, and judicial) Tj T*
(Proceedings of every other State. And the Congress may by general Laws prescribe the Manner in which) Tj T*
(such Acts, Records and Proceedings shall be proved, and the Effect thereof.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Citizens of each State shall be entitled to all Privileges and Immunities of Citizens in the) Tj T*
(several States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(New States may be admitted by the Congress into this Union; but no new State shall be formed or) Tj T*
(erected within the Jurisdiction of any other State; nor any State be formed by the Junction of two) Tj T*
(or more States, or Parts of States, without the Consent of the Legislatures of the States concerned) Tj T*
(as well as of the Congress.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The United States shall guarantee to every State in this Union a Republican Form of Government, and) Tj T*
(shall protect each of them against Invasion; and on Application of the Legislature, or of the) Tj T*
(Executive \(when the Legislature cannot be convened\) against domestic Violence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
(Evaluation fixture page 5) Tj T*
