(Article. V.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Congress, whenever two thirds of both Houses shall deem it necessary, shall propose Amendments) Tj T*
(to this Constitution, or, on the Application of the Legislatures of two thirds of the several) Tj T*
(States, shall call a Convention for proposing Amendments, which, in either Case, shall be valid to) Tj T*
(all Intents and Purposes, as Part of this Constitution, when ratified by the Legislatures of three) Tj T*
(fourths of the several States, or by Conventions in three fourths thereof, as the one or the other) Tj T*
(Mode of Ratification may be proposed by the Congress; Provided that no Amendment which may be made) Tj T*
(prior to the Year One thousand eight hundred and eight shall in any Manner affect the first and) Tj T*
(fourth Clauses in the Ninth Section of the first Article; and that no State, without its Consent,) Tj T*
(shall be deprived of its equal Suffrage in the Senate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
(Evaluation fixture page 6) Tj T*
ET
