(Article. VI.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All Debts contracted and Engagements entered into, before the Adoption of this Constitution, shall) Tj T*
(be as valid against the United States under this Constitution, as under the Confederation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This Constitution, and the Laws of the United States which shall be made in Pursuance thereof; and) Tj T*
(all Treaties made, or which shall be made, under the Authority of the United States, shall be the) Tj T*
(supreme Law of the Land; and the Judges in every State shall be bound thereby, any Thing in the) Tj T*
(Constitution or Laws of any State to the Contrary notwithstanding.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Senators and Representatives before mentioned, and the Members of the several State) Tj T*
(Legislatures, and all executive and judicial Officers, both of the United States and of the several) Tj T*
(States, shall be bound by Oath or Affirmation, to support this Constitution; but no religious Test) Tj T*
(shall ever be required as a Qualification to any Office or public Trust under the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source: National Archives - The Constitution of the United States - https://www.archives.gov/founding-docs/constitution) Tj T*
